--- !u!114 &1220964028
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1220964025}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a11dd23e08e5cb942a6a6b4da8d43711, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TEXDrawRuntime::TexDrawLib.TEXDraw
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_Alignment: {x: 0.5, y: 0.5}
  m_Text: "That\u2019s Correct!\r\n\r\nThere are 9 nurses and 4 physicians, so the
    total number of staff members is: 9 + 4 = 13\r\n\r\nWe want the probability that
    the selected person is a nurse or a female.\r\n\r\nFirst, identify each group:\r\n\r\nNurses:
    9\r\n\r\nMale nurses: 5 = so female nurses: (9 - 5 = 4)\r\n\r\nPhysicians: 4\r\n\r\nMale
    physicians: 1 = so female physicians: (4 - 1 = 3)\r\n\r\nNow determine the counts
    we need:\r\n\r\nNurses (Nurse): 9\r\n\nFemales (Females): (4 + 3 = 7)\r\n\nFemale
    nurses (Nurse \\cap Female): 4\r\n\r\nSince some people are counted in both groups
    (female nurses), we use the addition rule of probability:\r\n\r\nP(Nurse \\cup
    Female) = P(N) + P(F) - P(Nurse \\cap Female)\r\n\r\nSubstitute the values:\r\n\r\nP(Nurse
    \\cup Female) = \\frac{9}{13} + \\frac{7}{13} - \\frac{4}{13}\r\n\r\nP(Nurse
    \\cup Female) = \\frac{12}{13}\r\n\r\nTherefore, the probability that the selected
    person is a nurse or female is:\r\n\r\n\\frac{12}{13}\r\n\r\nSo, the probability
    of selecting someone who is either a nurse or a female (or both) is 12 out of
    13.\r\n\n"
  m_Size: 6
  m_ScrollArea:
    serializedVersion: 2
    x: 0
    y: 0
